I'm probably wrong, but it seems to me that ybu must not have a pause
between the y and bu, following the pattern of the abu, ebu, etc, because
if one *did* pause, it would be seen as "y" in its usual meaning (consider
-- if you wanted to say "the way to mark a word as being a character
instead was with the word....uh...'bu'" Since this could naturally come out
unwanted, if you didn't 'y' to be the hesitation marker in that one case,
you could never accidentally hesitate before saying the word bu, because it
would always  be considered the letteral 'y'.  Hence, when we really want
to talk about the letteral, we must not pause.

  As I said above, I may be completely wrong

          --gejyspa


